ss "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "30 July 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2173"} "Grand Palais Éphémère, Paris, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2006926"} "33 from 33 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Georgia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/143220"} "Tato Grigalashvili"] " was the favorite. World ranked #2 in June 2024, he had won the World Championship in 2022, 2023, and 2024, and the European Championships in 2020, 2022, and 2024."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/134778"} "Takanori Nagase"] " (JPN) was the defending gold medalist and also took bronze in this class at Rio 2016. He was trying to become the first judoka to repeat as gold medalist in this class. He was already one of only six to earn two medals at 81 kg. Nagase was bronze medalist at the 2022 and 2023 World Championships and had won seven titles at IJF Grand Slams since 2013."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Belgium’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/141019"} "Matthias Casse"] " was also highly considered. A bronze medalist at Tokyo 2020 in this class, he came to Tokyo as the defending World Champion, winning that title in 2021, was the silver medalist at the World Championships in 2019, 2022, and 2023, and had six titles at IJF Grand Slam events between 2020 and 2024."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Unfortunately, Nagase and Casse met in the quarter-finals, with Nagase winning by " [:em {} "waza-ari"] ", using " [:em {} "o-soto-gari"] ". Nagase and Grigalashvili met in the final, where Nagase defended his gold medal by " [:em {} "ippon"] ", with " [:em {} "tani-otoshi"] " after 2:48."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the first bronze medal match, Casse was defeated by Korea’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/153312"} "Lee Jun-Hwan"] ", who won with " [:em {} "ko-uchi-gari"] " after 4:48. In the second bronze medal match, Russian-born " [:a {:href "/athletes/146824"} "Somon Makhmadbekov"] " (TJK) defeated Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/153286"} "Antonio Esposito"] " by " [:em {} "ippon"] ", with " [:em {} "ura-gatame"] " after 1:24."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/134778"} "Takanori Nagase"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143220"} "Tato Grigalashvili"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GEO"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GEO.png"}] "GEO"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/153312"} "Lee Jun-Hwan"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KOR.png"}] "KOR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/146824"} "Somon Makhmadbekov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/TJK"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/TJK.png"}] "TJK"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/141019"} "Matthias Casse"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BEL.png"}] "BEL"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [: